      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a pervasive and cynical tactic used by powerful corporations to deflect responsibility for the societal costs of their profit-driven innovations. By framing massive job displacement as an \"inevitable technological tide,\" they successfully shift the burden of adaptation onto the individual worker and the state. This narrative allows them to reap the massive gains of automation while avoiding the necessary investment in retraining, social welfare, or labor protections.",
      "source": "target",
